{
  "id": "COMPOUND:14268 - PROTEIN:2272",
  "verbalization": "Benzocaine is implicated in the regulation of Disintegrin and metalloproteinase domain-containing protein 28 through a multi-step mechanism involving 4-(3-Pyridin-2-Yl-1h-Pyrazol-4-Yl)Quinoline. This compound acts as a target of benzocaine, which in turn influences the activity of the enzyme Glutamine--fructose-6-phosphate aminotransferase [isomerizing], and also directly targets HSVEC. The shared pathway involves 4-(3-Pyridin-2-Yl-1h-Pyrazol-4-Yl)Quinoline, which is a known modulator of the Disintegrin and metalloproteinase domain-containing protein 28. The evidence suggests that benzocaine may influence the expression or activity of this protein through the activation of 4-(3-Pyridin-2-Yl-1h-Pyrazol-4-Yl)Quinoline, which in turn affects the target protein. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for benzocaine in modulating the function of Disintegrin and metalloproteinase domain-containing protein 28, possibly through the regulation of enzyme activity or protein expression. The evidence is consistent with a mechanistic link, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
